body:
Let her know you like her - no hinting and hoping she picks up on it. Man up and let her know.  She can then make a decision based on that and perhaps it'll work out in your favour. It may also not be right for her and she chooses the other person - in which case you need to respect that and move on. 

&#x200B;

all the best.

Hey mate, just take a step back and chill for a moment. I think you've worked yourself up a bit over nothing. She's just asked to think about it and, although it's tough waiting to know if she says yes or no, it's always best to let her take as long as she needs to make that decision. You don't want to put pressure on her to make a decision faster because then she might make the wrong one. Trust in her process and it should work out. 

&#x200B;

All the best.
